<h3>Activity2: Let's Make a Line Plot</h3><p>From the group's ACTUAL data, determine minimum and maximum length. Select quarter-, half- or whole-inch tick intervals so every length falls at a marked point; stack ONE X per recorded item, label the horizontal axis <strong>length in inches</strong> and title the plot. Source students draft on a blank line then display a final poster. Teacher may join two blank-line masters, which are not copied here.</p>
